 say to them  when the president of our closest ally  uses a photo opportunity outside a  church to have peaceful protesters  blasted out the way look I haven't seen  the scene that you'll talk about but  look well when we think even our closest  friends closest partners and countries  with which we've got a long history as  now of course will raise those difficult  issues I probably don't have the same  latitude that that celebrities do but I  do understand Turkey because I'm like  there was Hamilton or anyone from the  BME  community who looks at that and wonders  what the world coming to though I share  that sense of distress and of course we  want to see America come together we  don't want to see it go back to what we  saw in the 60s and some of those  tensions and we'll work with our our  closest ally to see what more we can do  with anything to support that process I  mean when you look at the United States  and you see a president that talks about  America first who withdraws from the  World Health Organization in the middle  of a pandemic who rips up the Iran  nuclear deal do you think it's perhaps  time for the UK to reassess their status  as our most special ally actually I  think what British people would expect  is that we of course natural friendships  now and lines around the world but also  stand up with a British national  interest we made clear that actually we  still see that the World Health  Organization has a role to play yes  you want answers about how the  coronavirus started but we don't want to  rip up the whu-oh at a time of a global  health pandemic so I think that is a  good example where we just take a  different view and we'll be honest about  it  what are you envisage Britain's role is  in the world especially as we come out  of this pandemic with so much changed  well if you look at the how we talked  about global Britain part of that of  course is as we leave the EU forging  strong relations and making sure we good  European neighbors with our European  partners global Britain is also about us  being a force for good in the world  Prime Minister is hosting the GAVI  summit tomorrow which is this summit to  get us up to seven point four billion  dollars worth of funding for vaccine  development we're confident that that's  going to be a success we need to bring  other countries together in that  endeavor and I think it's a good example  of the UK's role bringing countries  together as a force for good in the  world and you know we're living and  breathing it right now and I think  there's a great opportunity for us in  the future to expand on that thank you  very much

